LinkedIn News Asia shared a post: Would you be mentored by someone less exp=
erienced than you?=20

Reverse mentoring, or being mentored by someone from a different, usually y=
ounger generation can offer insights into what is happening at other levels=
 of a company and can highlight knowledge and skill gaps, writes leadership=
 coach Margaret E. Ward.=20

It can also help to foster a stronger workplace culture by boosting inter-g=
enerational understanding. If younger people see their input is having an e=
ffect on the senior staff member, they can also feel more connected to thei=
r jobs and are more likely to speak up in future.

For people who try out reverse mentoring, it's key that the senior staff me=
mber has an agenda for each meeting and takes a structured approach, writes=
 Ward. An open and curious approach is also important for the senior staffe=
r, to make sure they get the most out of it.=20

